# <%= name %>

A Storybook playground for prototyping <%= framework === 'svelte' ? 'Svelte' : 'React' %> components with the pragma design system.

## Start

```sh
bun run storybook
```

Storybook opens on <http://localhost:6006>. Edit `src/Prototype/` and the story reloads.

## What is installed

- `@canonical/styles`: tokens, fonts, cascade layers and base styles, loaded once in `.storybook/styles.css`.
<% if (dsGlobal) { -%>
- `@canonical/<%= framework %>-ds-global`: the global components.
<% } -%>
<% if (dsGlobalForm) { -%>
- `@canonical/react-ds-global-form`: form fields built on react-hook-form; its stylesheet is loaded in `.storybook/styles.css`.
<% } -%>
<% if (dsApp) { -%>
- `@canonical/<%= framework %>-ds-app`: application layouts and app-tier components.
<% } -%>

## Add a component

```sh
pragma create component <%= framework %> src/MyComponent
```

The generated component, its stories and its styles follow the same conventions as the design system's own packages, and appear in Storybook straight away.

## Look things up

`pragma block lookup <Name>` shows a design-system component's anatomy and modifiers, and `pragma token lookup <name>` a token's values.

## Check

```sh
bun run check
```

Runs Biome and the type checker.
